  portrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 0d56b25141ca016488ae90e45ff0a0cb, type: 3}
  journalLore: Some who rode out against the dark never came home, and some came back wrong. The burning knights ride the edges of the forest where the old fires were, their horses smouldering under the plate, and anything they cut keeps burning.
  journalAdvice: 'Frost cuts deep into it, fire hardly at all. It charges from far off: step aside as it comes and strike its flank as it turns. Its blows burn, so don''t trade them. It frightens horses.'
  journalHabitat: The old barrows and the ground around them
